ine sex drugs and rock  and roll are very popular Double Down  Sandino is a professional DJ who has set  up shop in Second Life  I love clubbing but not any old clubs go  into clubs where they're alive mixed DJs  and my usual second life gangs what I  love the most  dance you're in luck  strip clubs proliferate in second life  and if you want to play out your own  personal sexual fantasy there are lots  of escort options at very reasonable  rates and just think about it in second  life you can be a gay man one day and a  straight woman the next the  possibilities are endless  so with all this diversity you think  it'd be fights breaking out all over the  place but the truth is that second life  is amazingly peaceful of course if  you're looking for violence you can find  that to most of all second life is a  massive social experiment and the people  that come here form all kinds of  communities some of which are furry if  someone says they're a furry it could  mean they just like animals or they  liked anthro that is human ish animal  type cartoons when they were a kid so  how does all this work it's simple  really the people who own the property  in second life make the rules if you  don't like nudity or people shooting at  you all you have to do is teleport  somewhere else it's very much like what  Robert Nozick imagined in Anarchy state  and utopia a plethora of alternate  societies communism is mostly dead in  real life but even the communists have a  happy home in second life and don't  worry these communists aren't gonna  throw you into a gulag they're not in  power and no one else seems to be either  so who exactly is in charge here hey  guys who's your leader I'm not sure we  have one  I'm my own leader nice to meet you  second life is interesting and I think  successful because of the freedom it  grants  to create their own entertainment I  would say it's fairly anarchistic and  that everyone more or less is allowed to  do what they want  so long as it does